ipt>        </div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n#### R\n```r\nm$diag$ppc_stat(stat = \"n_zero\")\n```\n\n#### Julia\n```julia\nm.diag.ppc_stat(stat=\"n_zero\")\n```\n:::\n\nThe vertical line is the observed number of zeros, the curve the number of zeros in simulated datasets. A plain Poisson model would put the line far to the right of the curve; the zero-inflated model should place it in the middle. See [Diagnostics](start/Diagnostics.qmd) for every posterior predictive plot.\n\n::: {.callout-note collapse=\"true\"}\n## More checks\n\n::: {.panel-tabset group=\"language\"}\n#### Python\n\n::: {#7304cc5a .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nm.diag.ppc_rootogram()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div>            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/2.7.5/MathJax.js?config=TeX-AMS-MML_SVG\"></script><script type=\"text/javascript\">if (window.MathJax && window.MathJax.Hub && window.MathJax.Hub.Config) {window.MathJax.Hub.Config({SVG: {font: \"STIX-Web\"}});}</script>                <script type=\"text/javascript\">window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-3.1.1.min.js\" integrity=\"sha256-HUEFyfiTnZJxCxur99FjbKYTvKSzwDaD3/x5TqHpFu4=\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>                <div id=\"97e3e422-bbc4-4280-aa81-9eb47097be1c\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:525px; width:100%;\"></div>            <script type=\"text/javascript\">                window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                if (document.getElementById(\"97e3e422-bbc4-4280-aa81-9eb47097be1c\")) {                    Plotly.newPlot(                        \"97e3e422-bbc4-4280-aa81-9eb47097be1c\",                        [{\"base\":[-0.05099744788678784,-0.057891587199234706,0.17014849480325012,-0.1211981024995854,0.13753687588250818,1.1048755586037733,-0.552506983294711,0.1816590212458495,0.04743416490252569,0.015811388300841